# Generated from: specs/17-guide-nontechnical-coordinators-through-setup-and-routine-work/requirements.md
Feature: Guide nontechnical coordinators through setup and routine work
  As a first-time or rotating volunteer coordinator
  I want the application to guide me through setup and routine work in familiar language
  So that I can maintain coverage confidently without technical training or separate documentation

  @SCN001
  Scenario: First-time coordinator publishes the first schedule from visible guidance
    Given an empty installation has group-local time support
    And an allowlisted coordinator has no product training or external instructions
    When the coordinator signs in and follows the one primary next action
    Then ordered steps explain the group time zone and request-approval policy
    And lead through first schedule entry and volunteer-facing review
    And require explicit publication confirmation
    And finish on routine coordinator home with no hidden setup flag

  @SCN002
  Scenario Outline: Routine home leads directly to attention
    Given <work> needs coordinator attention
    When the coordinator opens home
    Then the <label> card shows the authoritative count and up to three urgent examples
    And its plain-language link opens the filtered resolution page

    Examples:
      | work                                      | label                    |
      | pending requests                          | Requests to review       |
      | uncovered future commitments              | Open commitments         |
      | unconfirmed assignments                   | Waiting for confirmation |
      | failed messages for unended commitments   | Messages not sent        |

  @SCN003
  Scenario Outline: High-impact action requires fresh consequence confirmation
    Given a coordinator starts <action>
    When the review page is displayed
    Then affected people, local dates, slots, and consequences are plain text
    And Go back without changes performs no mutation
    When authoritative state changes before final confirmation
    Then the stale confirmation is rejected and updated details require review

    Examples:
      | action                |
      | shift publication     |
      | shift deactivation    |
      | assignment cancellation|
      | volunteer replacement |

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Coordinator chooses a known volunteer without retyping contact data
    Given an eligible known volunteer exists
    When the coordinator chooses Choose known volunteer
    And selects the labelled name and email
    Then no contact field must be retyped
    And a replacement preview appears before mutation
    When the coordinator confirms
    Then the server reloads the selected volunteer and performs the authoritative assignment command

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Invalid form remains recoverable
    Given a coordinator has entered valid and invalid values in one form
    When server validation fails
    Then every valid value remains entered
    And the exact invalid field has adjacent plain-language help
    And all errors appear in a summary
    And no stack, database, provider, raw identifier, JSON, or UTC-conversion text appears

  @SCN006
  Scenario: Mobile keyboard workflow remains complete
    Given a coordinator uses keyboard only at a 320 CSS-pixel viewport
    When they complete setup, filter routine work, choose a volunteer, review consequences, go back, and confirm
    Then focus and reading order follow the visual task order
    And all targets, labels, states, errors, and consequences remain available without color, hover, drag, hidden gestures, or horizontal page scrolling
